{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264731,"nonce":"7i4vC99SFIPpKrtAHh/XMqiz78o=","title":"switch on an enum with GADT-style constructors: `case P:` matches every value","message":"private enum C\u003cX\u003e { P:C\u003cPR\u003e; V:C\u003cVR\u003e; }\n    static function g\u003cX\u003e(c:C\u003cX\u003e) { switch c { case P: trace(\"P\"); case _: trace(\"other\"); } }\n    g(P); g(V);   // Haxe: P other   rayzor: P P\n\nConstructors declared with an explicit type (`P:C\u003cPR\u003e`) are not resolved as enum variants in the case, so `P` is treated as a capture and matches everything. Plain `enum D { DP; DV; }` works. Present at 52585dd3 (before the pattern work). Issue6413 passes only because it never calls with V.","files":null}]}